{"author": [{"collection_id": "Authors", "document_content": {"avatar": {"file_path": "_f68a99ffe9144467a917320028f1ce3b_/_50ac3cbb26fa4c21a9967e26675f94c5_/369c95fe5019b07e689d250a71b99f23e954b4b1e7288cc521f9534e2f1b26e3402000d0d9b0ec2b449c286617c23522d81fa4a5aad5de6e88a30a6f158b944d", "height": 212, "url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/WXzPP98RdDrDneOh7QCxSdNkjwk9_ACKefFU5vhW7DtED5EeHavMyWl7ttNSOzpRiLZqvYoZCQxVwxJ7Bi47CN8h4tj_nqxjuTsH1szGG5nt1dZgwtr1", "width": 212}, "name": "Susanna Zaraysky", "title": "Content Strategist, Fonts"}, "document_id": 6292121203769344, "document_label": null, "repo_id": "mio-example"}], "body_content": [{"code_snippet": [], "content": "<p>If you were a web designer in the early days of the Internet, you might remember that there were few &ldquo;web safe&rdquo; typefaces, such as Arial and Georgia. As a result, many websites looked similar. To use a new typeface, you had to embed small Flash files for each heading in your layout.</p>\n<p>Now with <a href=\"https://fonts.google.com/knowledge/glossary/web_font\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">web fonts</a> and <a href=\"https://fonts.google.com/knowledge/using_variable_fonts_on_the_web\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">variable fonts</a>, the situation has changed dramatically. Designers have many more typeface choices to customize their websites and brands.</p>\n<p>Here are some of the ways that variable fonts are changing type:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>They allow designers to create more nuanced and expressive typography with different weights, widths, and other axes.</li>\n<li>They can improve the performance of web pages by reducing the number of font files that need to be loaded.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Tobias Kunisch went from being a webmaster at Google in 2010 to being one of the co-founders of Google Fonts, whose mission is to provide open source fonts without charge. Kunisch spoke at the <a href=\"https://config.figma.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Figma Config Conference</a> in June 2023 in San Francisco about how fonts are like software and how they open up new digital design possibilities.</p>\n<p>Watch his talk on YouTube:</p>\n<div style=\"text-align: center; position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; max-width: 100%; height: 0;\"><iframe style=\"border-radius: 16px; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;\" src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/-27L7iqFocI?si=oWcbwfiRx1UJOkeu\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/materialdesign?sub_confirmation=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Subscribe to Material Design</a> for even more design-related videos.</p>", "image": [], "related_links": [], "table": [], "video": []}], "category": "2023", "hero": {"a11y_description": "Splitscreen: tobias and a screenshot of text in an app", "bordered": true, "caption": null, "case": null, "file": {"file_path": "_f68a99ffe9144467a917320028f1ce3b_/_f3e8a4f639ce4c5aafa231fcb8daa630_/2e728362671229af2c7a87691fc94ff422b1a4859b2d82fd64999947af99f673d036d7736041979c46d23130d3fcae789388639a662cc99d7eeb33d4e8b59a04", "height": 1384, "url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/UZDpLpdaA00MuMc0cBiRzQTG3zvUR-ZMHyI7LALYCBzw3ZA7hRxnb-bwy4GZS7yqJhAxbIBWtQMQiAO4saj2W2YgfA-LAyFU26Zu3ilF_4l_SB3YOTk", "width": 2461}}, "hero_card": false, "metadata": {"keywords": "fonts video how-to", "meta_robots": " ", "schema_structure": "{}", "share_description": "Catch up on Google Fonts' talk at Figma Config 2023", "share_image": {"file_path": "_f68a99ffe9144467a917320028f1ce3b_/_f3e8a4f639ce4c5aafa231fcb8daa630_/35fa0a72d7e29936b768974ad1be33031fb13a51d65f6eece8a68dce9b2eb29672c9c17d1a54d22c31b30df50b5c25713a4ac534cc60856431e32066813c6d01", "height": 1384, "url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/cYWxgKkl5jYw0JO4OcSphMsQnGslv1uF2079rHpqeGENxk3bJP1F1BR9ElV8FbaMlPxmedn0Ij0Kqi4zd5YEStoBXjYquDVYRR-wN16ZbcQ71mHMWQ", "width": 2461}, "share_title": "Video: Fonts are software"}, "published_date": "2023-08-24T13:00:00", "slug": "fonts-are-software-video", "subtitle": "Catch up on Google Fonts' talk at Figma Config 2023", "title": "Video: Fonts are software", "up_next": {"items": [{"collection_id": "UpNextItems", "document_content": {"image": {"file_path": "_f68a99ffe9144467a917320028f1ce3b_/_67af19389b5f45048ff0f3b64759ab41_/0fdd6e585c167efbb12841bc6d4196ffca44662c6928e583881041686d5ddedc14f8ae7ee78f05986c156c069a3e8b466c4909eee1c0a58ddd521629bb9dc38c", "height": 532, "url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/t53yjKYzXLUMbZdsIWnTsrbhcSXAvj8xuldbHZwR1Z1H6nv8b3qjPmzlw57P7MvenJIOQO7Z_ICNiLqog2O4yrlvpsi4c-GLh7SFLfj7uljAN3AkU44", "width": 1064}, "link": {"aria_label": null, "href": "/blog/google-fonts-pairing-figma", "label": "You Asked for it\u2014Here Are Some of Our Favorite Font Pairings", "open_new_window": false}, "section": "Material Blog", "title": "You Asked for it\u2014Here Are Some of Our Favorite Font Pairings"}, "document_id": 6482900635746304, "document_label": null, "repo_id": "mio-example"}, {"collection_id": "UpNextItems", "document_content": {"image": {"file_path": "_f68a99ffe9144467a917320028f1ce3b_/_67af19389b5f45048ff0f3b64759ab41_/7198ad8f886e7c74d9ee23d7324805ba0e0490aae49d6202e1269badf81278cbccfcbd0805b8a65ce1194529b273a97353fb325c4969454d17e19596d9b5ec7b", "height": 1800, "url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/rfU5zd4NIK8BgbEhrPx7A6s7JaCTejMdriC0S6SWBZ8LMpGtCrxzPxMRPJUBI61Ba_jRSv79BePfKBprun_QNScU76Nyqse25Yu1p5C-ExXG_f2MEg", "width": 2700}, "link": {"aria_label": null, "href": "/blog/shantell-martin-variable-font", "label": null, "open_new_window": false}, "section": "Material Blog", "title": "The Story of Shantell Sans"}, "document_id": 5976668181233664, "document_label": null, "repo_id": "mio-example"}, {"collection_id": "UpNextItems", "document_content": {"image": {"file_path": "_f68a99ffe9144467a917320028f1ce3b_/_67af19389b5f45048ff0f3b64759ab41_/92b74c588c798a7dc073ec8a25c9d4b57d893d91ed8284b17156e8a66bd0dcf8029eb73d3a028cb39c7dd9